{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation report for #15917 at exact clean pushed head 2a273cf8baabe5dcef0eec82cc6cf4f9a90ebc84 on request/ui-security-headers (one commit over main 5ff8d69c). internal/service/browser.go states the browser policy once: Content-Security-Policy \"default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'\", X-Frame-Options DENY, X-Content-Type-Options nosniff, Referrer-Policy no-referrer. BrowserHeaders applies it in Server.Handler and gs serve applies it outermost around the trusted-host check and the deadline wrapper, so UI pages, assets, JSON views, not-found answers and the composed refusals all carry it. Conditions: (1) TestEveryResponseClassCarriesTheBrowserPolicy asserts all four headers, the policy pinned as a literal, on a UI page, the icon asset, a JSON view, a JSON refusal, a not-found answer and the trusted-host refusal, through the same composition gs serve uses; TestEmbeddedUILoadsUnderTheBrowserPolicy fetches index.html and every script, stylesheet, icon and font it names through the served embed, refusing inline script, style or handlers, non-same-origin references, data: or remote URLs in the stylesheet, CSSOM or bundler style injection and string-built code in the bundle, and any script or stylesheet whose declared content type a nosniff browser would not accept; removing the middleware fails both. Verified against a live gs serve on a scratch repository: /, /favicon.svg, /v0/status, the bundle, and a request with Host evil.example all carry the four headers. (2) go vet ./... and go test -count=1 ./... green at this head (35 packages, exit 0); the embed is unchanged, since the bundle needs nothing the policy forbids (one module script, one stylesheet, same-origin fonts and icon, same-origin fetches, React inline styles through DOM properties). (3) Rests-On #15917 in the commit; review requested next citing original 94e903f1 and the 2026-08-11 assessment. (4) docs/reference/gs/serve.md, docs/how-to/deploy-a-resident.md and docs/reference/architecture.md state the policy where they describe the browser contract. Two adversarial read-only passes: the first found the production composition left the trusted-host refusal outside the policy and one bundle check vacuous against the minifier's quoting; both fixed in this head and confirmed on re-review, which records frame-ancestors and the CSP as correct for the shipped bundle. Known uncovered surface: the opt-in pprof listener, outside this request. Co-signed artifacts follow at cmd/gs and the three docs.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-security-headers","commit":"2a273cf8baabe5dcef0eec82cc6cf4f9a90ebc84","path":"internal/service"}}